fuse|burning-cord|NOUN|cord that carries ignition|A cord that burns along its length to carry ignition to an explosive charge.|ngòi nổ; dây cháy chậm|The diagram labels the fuse on an old ceremonial firework.|Sơ đồ ghi tên ngòi nổ trên một loại pháo lễ hội cổ.|Countable; this is the burning-cord sense, not the electrical safety device. A short fuse is also a separate figurative expression.|-
medication|medicine|NOUN|medicine used for treatment|Medicine used to treat an illness or health condition.|thuốc; thuốc điều trị|The patient brought a list of her medication to the appointment.|Người bệnh mang danh sách thuốc đang dùng tới buổi hẹn.|Usually uncountable for medicine collectively; on medication describes receiving treatment. Plural medications refers to different medicines.|0
ring|jewellery|NOUN|jewellery worn on a finger|A small band worn around a finger as jewellery.|nhẫn|He kept his grandfather's ring in a lined wooden box.|Anh giữ chiếc nhẫn của ông mình trong một chiếc hộp gỗ có lót bên trong.|Countable; a ring on someone's finger. This boundary concerns jewellery rather than any circular arrangement.|0
ring|bell-sound|VERB|make a bell-like sound|To make a clear sound like a bell, or cause a bell to make that sound.|reo; rung chuông|The doorbell rang twice while we were unpacking.|Chuông cửa reo hai lần khi chúng tôi đang dỡ đồ.|Intransitive a bell rings; transitive ring a bell. Past tense rang and past participle rung.|1
ring|telephone|VERB|contact by telephone|To telephone someone.|gọi điện|I'll ring the repair shop before taking the bicycle there.|Tôi sẽ gọi điện cho cửa hàng sửa chữa trước khi mang xe đạp tới đó.|Chiefly British; ring someone, without to before the person. Rang and rung are irregular forms.|2
ring|circular-arrangement|NOUN|circular band or arrangement|A circular band or an arrangement of things in a circle.|vòng; vòng tròn|The children placed a ring of stones around the toy castle.|Bọn trẻ xếp một vòng đá quanh lâu đài đồ chơi.|Countable; a ring of something names what forms the circle. Separate from a finger ring and a ringing sound.|3
sceptical|doubtful|ADJECTIVE|doubting a claim|Not easily convinced that a statement or idea is true or useful.|hoài nghi; chưa tin|Mai was sceptical about the plan until she saw the trial results.|Mai hoài nghi về kế hoạch cho tới khi thấy kết quả thử nghiệm.|Sceptical about or of something; skeptical is a common American spelling. Doubt does not imply refusing all evidence.|0
weigh|have-weight|VERB|have a particular weight|To have a particular weight.|nặng; có trọng lượng|The parcel weighs less than the empty suitcase.|Bưu kiện nhẹ hơn chiếc va-li rỗng.|Intransitive weigh an amount; normally simple forms for a present weight, as in it weighs two kilos.|0
weigh|measure-weight|VERB|find how heavy something is|To measure the weight of a person or thing.|cân; đo trọng lượng|The cook weighed the flour before mixing the dough.|Người đầu bếp cân bột mì trước khi trộn bột làm bánh.|Transitive weigh something; weighed is the regular past form. Distinct from merely having a weight.|1
